  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math> <mrow> <mi>S</mi> </mrow></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math><msup> <mi>S</mi> <mo>′</mo> </msup> </math> are the focii of the ellipse <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If <math><mi>B</mi></math> is one of the ends of one of the latus rectum, then the area (in sq. units) of the triangle <math> <mrow> <mi>B</mi><mi>S</mi><msup> <mi>S</mi> <mo>′</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
